{
  "description": "Visibility is decided by where code is written, never by who called it (spec/execution-model.md:383). The `repeat` body is STILL RUNNING when it calls `helper`, so a dynamically scoped runtime walking the caller's scopes finds `:temp` and prints `5` twice; a lexical one cannot see it at all. `:temp` is born in a block scope and a block encloses no procedure body, so the sealed boundary is not what hides it and the read is the ordinary `ol-undefined-var` (spec/error-model.md:102) rather than `ol-var-not-visible`. The sibling `a-name-only-a-top-level-block-binds-is-not-boundary-hidden` calls the procedure AFTER the block has ended, where a dead scope explains the failure on its own; this fixture is the live-block shape, where only lexical scoping does.",
